<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pactos de Mayo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1902</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as May Pacts</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pactos de Mayo were a set of agreements signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> and Chile on 28 May 1902. They submitted the two countries' border disputes to arbitration by the British crown, limited their naval armaments, and so ended a costly naval arms race that had threatened war in the Andes and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patagonia">Patagonia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pactos-de-mayo.jpg" alt="Pactos de Mayo" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Revista Caras y Caretas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Presidente_Riesco_y_Ministros_Terry_y_Donoso_Vergara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
